{% extends "base.html.jinja" %}
{% block content %}
<h1>Privacy policy</h1>
<p class="lede">
  Neither the {{ site_name }} website nor its iOS app collects personal data. There is no
  account, no analytics, no advertising, no tracking, and no third-party
  script or SDK in either.
</p>
<p class="muted">Last updated 2026-09-17. Covers this website and the {{ site_name }} iOS app.</p>

<h2 id="site">The website</h2>
<ul>
  <li>Every page is a plain static file. No cookies are set and no JavaScript
      runs.</li>
  <li>No page makes a request to any server other than the one serving it.</li>
  <li>Calendar feeds (.ics) are plain files; your calendar app downloads them
      directly. This site does not know who has subscribed.</li>
  <li>The site is hosted on GitHub Pages. Like any web host, GitHub receives
      standard request information (IP address, the page requested, time,
      browser type) to serve pages &mdash; see GitHub's
      <a href="https://docs.github.com/en/site-policy/privacy-policies/github-general-privacy-statement">privacy
      statement</a>. This site adds no collection on top of that.</li>
</ul>

<h2 id="app">The iOS app</h2>
<ul>
  <li><strong>What stays on your phone:</strong> the waters you favourite, the
      latest copy of the planting schedule, and a record of which listings the
      app has already alerted you about. These live only in the app's own
      storage on your device (and in your device backups, if you back up your
      phone). Deleting the app deletes them. They are never sent to the
      developer or anyone else.</li>
  <li><strong>The one network request:</strong> the app downloads the public
      planting-schedule file this website publishes, from GitHub Pages. The
      request carries no identifier and nothing about you or your favourites;
      as with any web request, the host sees the IP address it came from.
      Links to CDFW's map or to this site open in your browser.</li>
  <li><strong>Notifications:</strong> alerts are local notifications that iOS
      schedules on your device. There is no push service and no device
      token.</li>
  <li><strong>Purchases:</strong> the one-time in-app purchase is handled
      entirely by Apple. The developer does not receive your name, email
      address or payment details; Apple's privacy policy applies to the
      transaction.</li>
  <li><strong>App Store privacy label:</strong> Data Not Collected.</li>
</ul>

<h2 id="children">Children</h2>
<p>Nothing is collected from anyone, including children.</p>

<h2 id="changes">Changes</h2>
<p>If this policy changes, this page changes, and the date above with it.</p>

<h2 id="contact">Questions</h2>
{% if support_email %}
<p>Email <a href="mailto:{{ support_email }}">{{ support_email }}</a>.</p>
{% else %}
<p>See <a href="{{ root }}support/">support &amp; FAQ</a>.</p>
{% endif %}
{% endblock %}
